-- title:
--   Krull intersection for mathfrak m_S-powers in a module-finite algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring that is Noetherian and local, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_S$ denoted `maximalIdeal S`, and let $C$ be a nontrivial commutative ring equipped with an $S$-algebra structure such that $C$ is finite as an $S$-module. The assertion is that the infimum, over all natural numbers $n$, of the ideals of $C$ obtained by pushing forward the powers $\mathfrak m_S^n$ along the structure map $S \to C$ is the zero ideal: $\bigcap_{n \in \mathbb N} (\mathfrak m_S^n)\, C = 0$, where $(\mathfrak m_S^n)\,C$ denotes the image ideal `(maximalIdeal S ^ n).map (algebraMap S C)`, that is, the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_S^n$. Equivalently, no nonzero element of $C$ lies in $\mathfrak m_S^n C$ for every $n$, so that the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic filtration of $C$ is separated.
--
--   This is the Krull intersection theorem in the form needed for a module-finite algebra over a Noetherian local base: the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic topology on $C$ is Hausdorff. It is used in the proof that the Lubin–Tate coordinate on a deformation ring with Drinfeld level structure gives an injective algebra map into a power series ring, via [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.injective_algHom_powerSeries_of_universal_of_cover`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.injective_algHom_powerSeries_of_universal_of_cover).
